            <ArticleTitle>Endoscopic Plantar Fascia Debridement for Chronic Plantar Fasciitis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>545-51</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.cpm.2016.06.004</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0891-8422(16)30059-3</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>When conservative therapy fails for chronic plantar fasciitis, surgical intervention may be an option. Surgical techniques that maintain the integrity of the plantar fascia will have less risk of destabilizing the foot and will retain foot function. Endoscopic debridement of the plantar fascia can be performed reproducibly to reduce pain and maintain function of the foot.</AbstractText>
